*
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
*   SCREEN PAGE f, n
*
*   is compiled into
*
*   call !screen_page(f, n, ret, status)
*
*     f        the form (a collection from SCREEN FORM)
*     n        the page the widgets added from now on belong to: the number of a tab of the form's tab
*              strip (SCREEN TABS).  0 (or null) ends it: widgets added after that are on every page.
*     status   0; 1 if f is not a form or n is not a number (ELSE)
*
*   A widget on page n is drawn, can have the focus and takes keys only while tab n is the one chosen;
*   the others keep their values and SCREEN GET, SET and VALUES still reach them.  The tab strip itself,
*   labels and buttons that are to be seen on every page are added with the page at 0.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
subroutine screen_page(f, n, ret, status)
$catalog !screen_page

   ret = ''
   status = 1
   if jtype(f) # 'collection' then return
   if n # '' and not(num(n)) then return
   f{'curpage'} = n + 0
   status = 0

   return
end

* END-CODE
